From: dwong <dowling.wong@kit.edu>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:51:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] MLST: separate main paper and technical supplement; T22
 integrated everywhere

New entry points main_mlst.tex (23 pages of narrative, 9.6k words, journal
layout: 11pt/1in/1.05 against the preprint's 12pt/1.1in/1.15) and
supplement_mlst.tex (50 pages), with the extended arXiv preprint (main.tex, 116
pages) preserved unchanged as its own deliverable.

Main narrative: question and contributions; observation model and target risks;
recovery theory with Props. 3.2/3.3; estimator instances; controlled T19/T20/T21
evidence; instrument evidence including the unified three-instrument/three-
question table and T22; discussion and limitations.  Full derivations, proofs,
implementation detail, verification grids and the two three-panel diagnostic
figures moved to the supplement, which imports the main paper's labels via xr
and an alias table so shared appendix sources cross-reference real numbers (0
unresolved references in either build).

T22 integrated into both versions, both abstracts, the introduction
contributions, the discussion, the instrument table and claim rows 25/26, with
the verdicts reported as inconclusive and the estimates beside them.  Figure
generated/figures/fig_t22_narrowband.pdf added to make_part2_figures.py from the
compact export.

Evidence: scripts/export_t22.py writes evidence/data/paper1/t22_2026-09-11/
(7 files) from the verified run archive; scripts/recompute_t22.py re-derives
every interval, p-value and verdict from the archived draw arrays independently
of the report and reproduces them exactly.

Checks: claim validation 0 errors over 75 path references, 9/9 values re-read;
evidence manifest 259 files complete; all four documents build with 0 undefined
references and 0 overfull boxes above 3.4pt.

