+\paragraph{Narrowband representation at the same window, predeclared and
+executed once (T22).}
+The whole-window stage left one hypothesis: that the failure was estimation
+error in a $65\,536$-dimensional subspace fitted from $350$ windows.  T22 tests
+it by removing that factor and keeping everything else --- same window length,
+endpoint, truth labels, transfer calibration, rank, baselines, bootstrap and
+reporting --- and fitting the rank-2 subspace instead on the $2B$ real
+coordinates of the $B$ unitary-DFT bins centred on the injection bin.  Two
+freezes are recorded: a stage-0 protocol
+(\nolinkurl{plan/T22_STAGE0_PROTOCOL_2026-09-11.md} and its JSON) written before
+any code, and a selected-band predeclaration
+(\nolinkurl{reviews/2026-09-11-PREDECLARED_T22.md}) written before any hold-out
+outcome was scored.  The hold-out stretches are \emph{new time regions} of files
+already examined, starting at sample $37\,027\,840$ --- the whole-window stretch
+end plus two guards, so they do not overlap --- which makes this a temporal
+hold-out and \emph{not} independent-file replication.  $B=1$ is the identity
+control (a rank-2 projector on two real coordinates is the identity, so
+band-PCA $=$ band-EMPCA $=$ bin read); it was asserted to a relative $10^{-12}$
+on all six development stretches and measured between $-1.2\times10^{-18}$ and
+$+2.9\times10^{-17}$.  The declared rule --- the smallest admissible candidate
+within one paired-bootstrap standard deviation of the best --- selected $B=9$,
+giving $p/n=18/350=0.051$ against $187$.
+
+The dimensional hypothesis is confirmed in direction.  Over the seven eligible
+stretches the learned rank-2 reconstruction's mean amplitude RMSE falls from
+$0.655$ to $0.249$ while the zero predictor stays at $0.654$--$0.689$ and the
+bin read at $0.246$--$0.261$: it moves from indistinguishable from predicting
+zero, and $2.7\times$ worse than a bin read, to \emph{better} than the bin read
+(Fig.~\ref{fig:t22-narrowband}).  On the frozen final test the equal-file
+contrast $\overline{\Delta}(\text{bin read},\text{band-EMPCA})$ is
+$+1.58\times10^{-3}$ $[+3.5\times10^{-4},+3.2\times10^{-3}]$, positive on all
+four eligible files with each file's own interval excluding zero; validation
+gave the same direction.
+
+\emph{All three registered verdicts are nevertheless \textbf{inconclusive}.}
+The frozen dependence assessment did not stabilise --- the aggregate
+block-variance curve is still rising at the largest usable block,
+$V(32)/V(16)=1.745$, leaving nine complete blocks, the same limiting count as
+the whole-window stage's $150/16$ --- and the rule declared before development
+withholds every benefit verdict in that case, not only the limited-recovery
+one.  Had it stabilised, limited recovery ($+0.3927$ $[+0.0045,+0.798]$ against
+zero and $+0.3935$ $[+0.0046,+0.798]$ against the calibration mean; Holm-adjusted
+$p=0.020$) and denoising benefit ($p=6.0\times10^{-4}$) would have been declared
+and metric contribution would not.
+
+The metric contribution is absent:
+$\overline{\Delta}(\text{band-PCA},\text{band-EMPCA})=-3.8\times10^{-5}$
+$[-2.3\times10^{-4},+1.3\times10^{-4}]$, $p=0.70$, with the point estimate
+marginally favouring band-PCA, so the registered direction is \emph{not met}.
+The explanation is post hoc but structural: the two differ only in the metric,
+and inside a nine-bin band the noise PSD is nearly flat.  The measured in-band
+dynamic range $\max_kN_k/\min_kN_k$ is $1.16$--$4.66$ across the eight hold-out
+stretches against $4.77\times10^{4}$ over the interior bins of the whole
+window.  The restriction that fixes the estimation problem therefore removes
+most of the metric's leverage --- the paper's two determinants trading off
+against each other --- and whether a band wide enough to carry PSD structure
+and narrow enough to keep $p/n$ small exists on this instrument is untested.
+File \texttt{0016}, eligible at the whole window, is \emph{chirped} in the new
+time region (drift $5.54$ bins against the declared $0.5$) and is excluded by
+the declared rule, leaving four eligible final-test files; the
+inverse-variance combination is again dominated by one file ($I^2=0.986$), which
+is why the equal-file mean is primary; and the equal-file $t$-interval on the
+point estimates alone includes zero on every contrast while the two-stage
+bootstrap excludes it on three.  $240$ of a declared cap of $250$ fits were
+spent.  The full report, including the one amendment made on development
+material and the deterministic re-score that followed, is
+\nolinkurl{reviews/2026-09-11-T22-report.md}.
+
