+# T22 — narrowband TIDMAD at the long window, 11 September 2026
+
+Compact export of the frozen T22 run, written by `scripts/export_t22.py` from
+the experiment repository's full run tree
+`results/t22_2026-09-11/{T22_characterize_v1, T22_development_v1,
+T22_development_v2, T22_freeze_v1, T22_validation_v1, T22_final_test_v1}` on
+branch `mlst/t22-2026-09-11`.  Every stage output was verified against its own
+`RESULTS_SHA256` before anything here was written; the digests are in
+`frozen.json → stage_output_sha256`.  Nothing here is recomputed.
+
+| file | content |
+|---|---|
+| `per_file.csv` | one row per evaluated hold-out stretch: characterisation, the four primary contrasts with joint block-bootstrap intervals and standard deviations, eligibility, file verdict, RMSE by method |
+| `combined.csv` | one row per contrast: the equal-file primary with its two-stage bootstrap interval and p-value, the three secondary sensitivities, and the validation-stage primary beside it |
+| `rmse_by_method.csv` | mean amplitude RMSE by method over the seven eligible stretches (validation + final test) |
+| `band_selection.csv` | the development band grid, the paired-bootstrap standard deviations, and which candidate the declared rule selected |
+| `dependence.csv` | the aggregate normalised block-variance curve behind the dependence verdict |
+| `verdicts.json` | the three registered verdicts with every decision input (p-values raw and Holm-adjusted, dependence verdict, file counts, fit counts) |
+| `frozen.json` | the frozen configuration, file roles, seeds, and the code/config/input SHA-256 hashes |
+
+**Not exported, retained in the experiment repository:** the per-file
+bootstrap draw arrays (`t22_validation_draws.npz`, `t22_final-test_draws.npz`;
+33 and 55 arrays of 2000 replicates each) and the full stage JSONs with their
+dependence curves, autocorrelations and per-window diagnostics.  The draw
+arrays are what a local reviewer needs to recompute the combined intervals and
+p-values from scratch; they are listed in the handoff synchronization
+inventory.
+
+**Reading order.** The protocol is `plan/T22_STAGE0_PROTOCOL_2026-09-11.md`
+and its JSON; the selected-band freeze is
+`reviews/2026-09-11-PREDECLARED_T22.md`; the report is
+`reviews/2026-09-11-T22-report.md`.
+
+**All three verdicts are `inconclusive`**, because the frozen dependence
+assessment did not stabilise and amendment A3 — declared before development —
+withholds every benefit verdict in that case.  The estimates, intervals and
+p-values are reported in full beside them.  Do not read a verdict off the
+intervals alone.
