+\subsection{TIDMAD: a narrowband representation at the same window}
+\label{subsec:mlst-t22}
+
+The whole-window stage left one hypothesis: that the failure was estimation
+error in a $65\,536$-dimensional subspace fitted from $350$ windows.  T22 tests
+it by removing exactly that factor and keeping everything else --- the same
+window length, endpoint, truth labels, transfer calibration, rank, baselines,
+bootstrap and reporting.  Only the space the rank-2 subspace is fitted in
+changes: from the whole window to the $2B$ real coordinates of the $B$
+unitary-DFT bins centred on the injection bin.
+
+\paragraph{Design, in two recorded freezes.}
+A stage-0 protocol fixed the allocation, representation, estimators, selection
+rule, admissibility, eligibility branches, dependence policy, inference,
+multiplicity and budget \emph{before any code was written}; a selected-band
+predeclaration fixed $B$, the block lengths, the dependence verdict, the file
+roles and every code and input hash \emph{before any hold-out outcome was
+scored}.  Each stretch is $64$ transfer-calibration $+$ $350$ fit $+$ $300$
+evaluation windows with $16\,384$-sample guards, $46\,825\,472$ samples in all.
+Hold-out stretches are \emph{new time regions} of files already examined ---
+starting at sample $37\,027\,840$, which is the whole-window stretch end plus
+two guards, so there is no overlap --- and this is a temporal hold-out, not
+independent-file replication.  $B=1$ is the identity control: a rank-2
+projector on two real coordinates is the identity, so band-PCA $=$ band-EMPCA
+$=$ bin read, asserted to a relative $10^{-12}$ on all six development
+stretches and measured between $-1.2\times10^{-18}$ and $+2.9\times10^{-17}$.
+$B=9$ was selected on development by the declared rule --- the smallest
+admissible candidate whose equal-stretch mean is within one paired-bootstrap
+standard deviation of the best (Fig.~\ref{fig:mlst-t22}c) --- giving $p/n=18/350=0.051$
+against the whole window's $187$.
+
+\paragraph{The dimensional hypothesis is confirmed in direction.}
+Over the seven eligible stretches the mean amplitude RMSE of the learned rank-2
+reconstruction falls from $0.655$ to $0.249$, while the zero predictor stays at
+$0.654$--$0.689$ and the bin read at $0.246$--$0.261$
+(Fig.~\ref{fig:mlst-t22}a).  The learned reconstruction moves from
+\emph{indistinguishable from predicting zero and $2.7\times$ worse than a bin
+read} to \emph{better than the bin read}.  On the frozen final test the
+equal-file contrast $\overline{\Delta}(\text{bin read},\text{band-EMPCA})$ is
+$+1.58\times10^{-3}$ $[+3.5\times10^{-4},+3.2\times10^{-3}]$, positive on all
+four eligible files with each file's own interval excluding zero, and the
+validation stage gave the same direction ($+1.82\times10^{-2}$
+$[+2.5\times10^{-3},+3.1\times10^{-2}]$).
+
+\paragraph{All three verdicts are nevertheless inconclusive.}
+The frozen dependence assessment did not stabilise --- the aggregate
+block-variance curve is still rising at the largest usable block,
+$V(32)/V(16)=1.745$, leaving nine complete blocks, the \emph{same} limiting
+count as the whole-window stage's $150/16$ --- and the rule declared before
+development withholds every benefit verdict in that case, not only the
+limited-recovery one.  Table~\ref{tab:mlst-t22} reports the three claims with
+what their estimates and intervals would have said.  Two would have been
+declared (limited recovery, Holm-adjusted $p=0.020$; denoising benefit,
+$p=6.0\times10^{-4}$) and one would not.
+
+\paragraph{The metric contribution is absent, and there is a structural
+reason.}
+The combined contrast is
+$\overline{\Delta}(\text{band-PCA},\text{band-EMPCA})=-3.8\times10^{-5}$, with
+interval $[-2.3\times10^{-4},+1.3\times10^{-4}]$ and $p=0.70$: the point
+estimate marginally favours band-PCA, and the registered direction is
+\emph{not met}.
+The explanation is post hoc but structural: band-PCA and band-EMPCA differ only
+in the metric, and inside a nine-bin band the noise PSD is nearly flat, so the
+whitening weight is nearly proportional to the identity.  The measured
+in-band dynamic range $\max_k N_k/\min_k N_k$ is $1.16$--$4.66$ across the eight
+hold-out stretches, against $4.77\times10^{4}$ over the interior bins of the
+whole window --- four orders of magnitude less for the metric to act on.  This
+is the interesting negative result of the stage: \textbf{the same restriction
+that fixes the estimation problem removes most of the metric's leverage}, so
+the paper's two determinants trade off against each other here.  Whether a band
+wide enough to carry PSD structure and narrow enough to keep $p/n$ small exists
+on this instrument is untested; the four candidates do not span it.
+
