+# T22 — narrowband representation at the long TIDMAD window: report
+
+_11 September 2026.  Executed on the KIT server against
+`/ceph/dwong/paper1_dataset/tidmad/raw`.  Stage-0 protocol:
+[`plan/T22_STAGE0_PROTOCOL_2026-09-11.md`](../plan/T22_STAGE0_PROTOCOL_2026-09-11.md)
+and its JSON.  Selected-band freeze:
+[`reviews/2026-09-11-PREDECLARED_T22.md`](2026-09-11-PREDECLARED_T22.md).
+Compact evidence: `evidence/data/paper1/t22_2026-09-11/`._
+
+## 0. The three verdicts
+
+| claim | contrast(s) | equal-file estimate | 95 % interval | raw p | Holm p | **verdict** |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| limited recovery | Δ(zero, band-EMPCA) | +0.392717 | [+0.00453, +0.798] | 0.0102 | 0.0204 | **inconclusive** |
+| | Δ(cal-mean, band-EMPCA) | +0.39348 | [+0.00455, +0.798] | 0.008399 | | |
+| denoising benefit | Δ(bin read, band-EMPCA) | +0.00158297 | [+0.000352, +0.00324] | 0.0002 | 0.0005999 | **inconclusive** |
+| metric contribution | Δ(band-PCA, band-EMPCA) | -3.78809e-05 | [-0.000231, +0.00013] | 0.6987 | 0.6987 | **inconclusive** |
+
+**All three verdicts are `inconclusive`, and that is the declared rule applying
+as written.**  The frozen dependence assessment did not stabilise, and
+amendment A3 — recorded before development ran — withholds every benefit
+verdict in that case, not only the limited-recovery one.  The estimates,
+intervals and p-values above are reported in full and are not verdicts.
+
+Read separately from the withholding, the numbers say three different things:
+
+* **Limited recovery.**  Both intervals exclude zero in band-EMPCA's favour and
+  the Holm-adjusted p is 0.0204 < 0.05.  Had the dependence
+  assessment stabilised, this claim would have been declared.
+* **Denoising benefit.**  The interval excludes zero and the Holm-adjusted p is
+  0.0006; the contrast is positive on **all four** eligible
+  final-test files individually, each with its own interval excluding zero.
+  This is the open question of the design, and it points one way.
+* **Metric contribution.**  The point estimate marginally favours band-**PCA**,
+  the interval includes zero and p = 0.699.  The registered direction
+  (band-EMPCA better than band-PCA, as found at the whole window) is **not
+  met**.  Section 6 gives the structural reason.
+
+## 1. What changed, and what it shows
+
+T10–T12 evaluated a rank-2 subspace on the **whole** 65 536-sample window and
+found no useful recovery: the learned reconstructions sat at the level of
+predicting zero and were about 2.7× worse than reading the injection bin.  The
+diagnosed cause was dimensional — 65 536 real coordinates against 350 fit
+windows, p/n = 187.  T22 removes exactly that factor and keeps everything else:
+same window length, endpoint, labels, transfer calibration, rank, baselines,
+bootstrap and reporting; only the space the subspace is fitted in changes, to
+the 2B real coordinates of the B unitary-DFT bins centred on the injection bin.
+
+At the selected B = 9 the ratio is p/n = 18/350 = 0.051, a factor of
+3.6 × 10³ smaller.  The measured consequence, over the seven eligible
+stretches of validation and the final test:
+
+| method | mean amplitude RMSE, **narrowband B = 9** | mean amplitude RMSE, **whole window** (T10–T12, 11 stretches) |
+|---|---|---|
+| zero | 0.6891 | 0.6544 |
+| cal. mean | 0.6910 | 0.6578 |
+| band PCA | 0.2486 | 0.6614 |
+| band EMPCA | 0.2493 | 0.6550 |
+| bin read | 0.2610 | 0.2455 |
+| quad. OF | 0.2610 | 0.2455 |
+| Wiener | 0.2527 | 0.2427 |
+| shrink. cal. | 0.2532 | 0.2408 |
+
+The learned rank-2 reconstruction moves from *indistinguishable from predicting
+zero and 2.7× worse than a bin read* to **better than the bin read**
+(0.2493 against 0.2610), while the zero predictor stays where it was.  That is
+the dimensional hypothesis of the whole-window stage confirmed in direction, on
+a temporal hold-out, at the same window length and rank.
+
+**What this is not.**  The hold-out files are new *time regions* of files
+already examined in T10–T12; this is a temporal hold-out, **not**
+independent-file replication.  Four eligible final-test files is a small
+number.  And the verdicts are withheld, so none of the three claims is
+declared.
+
+## 2. Design and freezes
+
+Two freezes, both recorded before the outcomes they govern.  The stage-0
+protocol fixed the allocation, representation, estimators, selection rule,
+admissibility, eligibility branches, dependence policy, inference, multiplicity
+and budget before any T22 code was written.  The selected-band predeclaration
+fixed B, the block lengths, the dependence verdict, the file roles and all code
+and input hashes before any hold-out outcome was scored.
+
+Allocation per stretch: 64 transfer-calibration + guard + 350 fit + guard + 300
+evaluation windows of 65 536 samples = 46 825 472 samples (4.68 s).  Hold-out
+stretches start at sample 37 027 840 = 36 995 072 (the T10 stretch end) + 2 ×
+16 384, so they do not overlap prior exposure.  Estimators: zero,
+calibration-mean, bin read, quadrature OF, band-PCA, band-EMPCA, Wiener,
+calibration shrinkage — only the two learned ones see the band.
+
+### The B = 1 identity control
+
+Asserted on all six development stretches at relative tolerance 10⁻¹²:
+band-PCA = band-EMPCA = bin read, because a rank-2 projector on two real
+coordinates is the identity.  Measured Δ(bin read, band-EMPCA) at B = 1 ranged
+from −1.2 × 10⁻¹⁸ to +2.9 × 10⁻¹⁷.  The runner aborts on failure.
+
+### Band selection (development only)
+
+| B | admissible | equal-stretch mean Δ(bin read, band-EMPCA) | paired-bootstrap sd | 95 % CI | |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 3 | yes | +0.004326 | 0.000575 | [+0.00324, +0.00550] | |
+| 5 | yes | +0.005387 | 0.000659 | [+0.00409, +0.00666] | |
+| 9 | yes | +0.005636 | 0.000710 | [+0.00422, +0.00701] | **selected** |
+| 17 | yes | +0.006109 | 0.000677 | [+0.00477, +0.00739] | *best* |
+
+Rule: the smallest admissible candidate within one paired-bootstrap standard
+deviation of the best.  Best = 17; threshold = 0.006109 − 0.000677 = 0.005432;
+smallest admissible candidate at or above it = **9** (B = 5 falls short at
+0.005387).  The bootstrap pairs candidates inside each replicate — one
+calibration-block and one evaluation-block resample per stretch, `ĝ` refitted
+once, then every candidate recomputed from those same indices.
+
+## 3. The dependence verdict
+
+The aggregate normalised block-variance curve over the development stretches:
+
+| block length | normalised variance (max over 220 curves) |
+|---|---|
+| 1 | 1.000 |
+| 2 | 2.089 |
+| 4 | 4.327 |
+| 8 | 7.491 |
+| 16 | 15.938 |
+| 32 | 27.816 |
+
+The variance is **still rising at the largest usable block**: adjacent ratios
+[2.089, 2.072, 1.731, 2.128, 1.745], V(32)/V(16) = 1.745, so the declared
+plateau rule returns `inconclusive`.  Per curve the picture is mixed
+({'inconclusive': 107, 'stabilised': 112, 'stabilised-at-endpoint': 1}); the declared decision is taken on the
+aggregated maximum curve, which is conservative by construction.  The
+calibration curve is inconclusive too (b = 8).
+
+This is the outcome the Part II audit anticipated.  300 evaluation windows at
+block 32 leave nine complete blocks — the *same* limiting count as T10's
+150/16.  The longer evaluation set widened the diagnosable range without
+resolving the dependence problem, and amendment A3 applies the withholding to
+all three claims rather than to limited recovery alone.
+
+## 4. Per-file results at B = 9
+
+| file | stage | outcome | f (kHz) | Δ(zero, E) | Δ(bin read, E) | 95 % CI | Δ(PCA, E) | 95 % CI | in combined |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `0012` | validation | eligible-coupled | 160.1 | +0.55675 | +0.028117 | [+0.02005, +0.03783] | -0.00087258 | [-0.002188, +0.000472] | yes |
+| `0013` | validation | eligible-coupled | 310.1 | -0.009689 | +0.024424 | [+0.01368, +0.03562] | -0.0045782 | [-0.007752, -0.001332] | yes |
+| `0014` | validation | eligible-coupled | 470.0 | +1.9736 | +0.0021321 | [-0.0005345, +0.005006] | +0.0001262 | [-3.228e-05, +0.0002911] | yes |
+| `0015` | final-test | eligible-coupled | 620.0 | +0.9618 | +0.0038751 | [+0.001754, +0.005878] | +0.00014594 | [-0.0001172, +0.0004013] | yes |
+| `0016` | final-test | chirped | 780.0 | +0.50896 | +0.0018668 | [-0.0002798, +0.004136] | -6.1328e-05 | [-0.0002621, +0.0001363] | no |
+| `0017` | final-test | eligible-coupled | 930.0 | +0.5992 | +0.0013035 | [+0.0005185, +0.002047] | -0.00029257 | [-0.0005512, -5.366e-05] | yes |
+| `0018` | final-test | eligible-coupled | 1799.9 | -0.00076978 | +0.0010688 | [+0.0009433, +0.001203] | -1.047e-05 | [-2.828e-05, +9.081e-06] | yes |
+| `0019` | final-test | eligible-coupled | 3400.0 | +0.010639 | +8.4495e-05 | [+4.984e-05, +0.0001199] | +5.5756e-06 | [-1.426e-05, +2.162e-05] | yes |
+
+`0016` was eligible-coupled in the T10 time region but is **chirped** in the new
+one (drift 5.543 bins over the stretch against the declared 0.5), so by the
+declared rule it is evaluated, reported and excluded from every combined
+estimate.  That leaves four eligible final-test files — exactly the declared
+threshold below which a combined interval would have been labelled indicative
+only.
+
+Δ(bin read, band-EMPCA) is positive on **all seven** eligible stretches and its
+own interval excludes zero on six of them (`0014` includes zero).  Δ(PCA,
+band-EMPCA) is negative on four of seven — band-PCA slightly better — and its
+interval excludes zero on two, in opposite directions (`0013` favours PCA,
+`0017` favours PCA).
+
+## 5. Combined inference
+
+Primary: the equal-file mean over the eligible final-test files, with a
+two-stage percentile bootstrap (10 000 replicates, seed 20260911) that
+resamples files and, within each drawn file, draws from that file's own
+joint-bootstrap replicate array — so within-file calibration and block
+uncertainty enters the file-level interval.  Secondary sensitivities are
+reported beside it and are never the headline.
+
+| contrast | equal-file primary | 95 % CI | p | inverse-variance | random effects | equal-file t-interval |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Δ(zero, empca) | +0.39272 | [+0.004527, +0.7975] | 0.0102 | -0.0007612 [-0.000828, -0.000694] | +0.1991 [+0.163, +0.236] | [-0.358, +1.14] |
+| Δ(calibration-mean, empca) | +0.39348 | [+0.004551, +0.798] | 0.008399 | -0.0004552 [-0.000782, -0.000129] | +0.1998 [+0.163, +0.237] | [-0.358, +1.15] |
+| Δ(raw-bin, empca) | +0.001583 | [+0.0003517, +0.003236] | 0.0002 | +0.0001528 [+0.000119, +0.000187] | +0.001092 [+0.000293, +0.00189] | [-0.000989, +0.00416] |
+| Δ(pca, empca) | -3.78809e-05 | [-0.0002314, +0.0001296] | 0.6987 | -2.726e-06 [-1.57e-05, +1.02e-05] | -4.602e-06 [-3.53e-05, +2.61e-05] | [-0.00033, +0.000254] |
+
+Two features of that table matter.  The **inverse-variance combination is again
+essentially one file** — I² = 0.986 on the denoising contrast, Q = 216.0 on 3 df —
+which is exactly why the 11 September amendment made the equal-file mean
+primary.  And the **equal-file t-interval on the point estimates alone includes
+zero** on every contrast, while the two-stage bootstrap excludes it on three:
+with four files and t₃ = 3.182 the t-interval is very wide, and the two
+intervals answer different questions (the t-interval treats each file's point
+estimate as one observation and discards its within-file precision; the
+two-stage bootstrap keeps it).  Both are reported; neither is a verdict.
+
+Multiplicity: Holm–Bonferroni step-down at familywise 0.05 over the three
+claims, with the limited-recovery claim taking the larger of its two
+constituent p-values.  Validation (three files, `0012`/`0013`/`0014`) gave
+Δ(bin read, E) = +0.018292 [+0.0025, +0.03084], p = 0.0004, i.e. the same
+direction; its combined interval was labelled indicative only (three files).
+
+## 6. Why the metric contribution vanished — a structural explanation, post hoc
+
+Band-PCA and band-EMPCA differ only in the metric.  Inside a nine-bin band the
+noise PSD is nearly flat, so the whitening weight is nearly proportional to the
+identity and the two fits nearly coincide.  Measured on the science-file noise
+bin powers, the ratio max(N_k)/min(N_k) across the selected band is **1.16 to
+4.66** on the eight hold-out stretches, against **4.77 × 10⁴** across the
+interior bins of the whole window — four orders of magnitude less dynamic range
+for the metric to act on.
+
+This is a structural consequence of the narrowband design, not a defect, and it
+is the interesting negative result of T22: **the same restriction that fixes
+the estimation problem removes most of the metric's leverage.**  The two
+determinants of the paper — metric and class — trade off against each other
+here.  This explanation is post hoc; it was not registered, and it is stated as
+an explanation of these runs, not as a validated law.  A design that separates
+the two would need a band wide enough to carry PSD structure and narrow enough
+to keep p/n small, which the four candidates tested do not span.
+
+## 7. Deviations, amendments and exposures
+
+| id | what | when |
+|---|---|---|
+| A1 | development set extended from 3 to 6 stretches; full band grid on the first four eligible in a declared order; nominal fits 184 → 240 (cap 250 unchanged) | stage 0, before any code |
+| A2 | evaluation block grid gains 32 | stage 0, before any code |
+| A3 | dependence withholding applies to all three benefit verdicts; primary combined interval becomes a two-stage bootstrap | stage 0, before any code |
+| A4 | second-line admissibility restated as a local-maximum test beyond a one-bin guard | on development material, before any hold-out outcome was read |
+
+**A4 in detail**, because it is the one amendment made after data were seen.
+The first form of the test compared the observed band power against the
+idealised boxcar Dirichlet skirt of a single tone, and rejected every band of
+width ≥ 3 on three of the four eligible development stretches.  Inspection of
+the measured profiles showed the reason: at B = 17 every profile decays
+monotonically outward on both sides — the signature of leakage, not of a second
+line — but real skirts sit about four times above the idealisation
+(rectangular-window leakage plus sub-bin frequency jitter across the 64
+calibration windows).  The test as written measured *"is the skirt wider than
+ideal"*, not *"is there a second line"*.  The restated test flags a band bin
+beyond the one-bin guard that carries ≥ 10 % of the line bin power **and** is a
+local maximum against its inward neighbour; it flags nothing on any development
+stretch, and a synthetic control confirms it still catches a genuine second tone
+three bins out at 30 % of the main line.  Development was re-scored once with
+identical seeds and inputs: **all contrasts reproduce exactly (0 differences,
+maximum absolute difference 0.0)**, so this was a deterministic re-score and not
+a new statistical evaluation.  Both runs are archived (`T22_development_v1`
+superseded, `T22_development_v2` canonical).
+
+**One post-processing correction, zero fits.**  The first summarisation of
+both hold-out stages reported, under the field name
+`equal_file_mean_of_point_estimates`, the equal-file mean of each file's
+*bootstrap* mean rather than of its *observed* contrast.  The label was wrong,
+not the inference: the intervals, p-values, Holm adjustment and all three
+verdicts are unchanged, and the two summaries differ only by the bootstrap's own
+small bias (for example `+0.39202` against `+0.392717` on Δ(zero, band-EMPCA)).
+A `recombine` stage was added that reads an archived stage output and its draw
+arrays and recomputes the combined block; it opens no data file and fits nothing
+(`fits_performed: 0`).  It was run once on each hold-out stage, writing
+`T22_validation_v2` and `T22_final_test_v2` and leaving `*_v1` untouched.  The
+numbers in this report and in the manuscript are the recombined ones.  A
+regression test now asserts that the two point summaries are different
+quantities and that the estimand field is `NaN` rather than silently substituted
+when the observed estimates are not supplied.
+
+**Exposure record.**  (1) T10–T12 read `[7 097 152, 44 092 224)` of
+`0000`/`0005`/`0010` and `[0, 36 995 072)` of every other validation file.
+(2) T22 characterisation read the 64 transfer-calibration windows of all eleven
+T22 stretches and fitted no method.  (3) T22 development scored 22 cells on six
+development stretches, twice (v1 and v2, identical contrasts).  (4) Validation
+and the final test each ran once.  No smoke run touched instrument data.  No
+hold-out stretch was scored before the freeze file existed; the runner refuses
+to start those stages without it.
+
+**Fit accounting.**
+
+| stage | fits |
+|---|---|
+| characterisation | 0 |
+| development (counted scientifically; executed twice) | 176 |
+| validation | 24 |
+| final test | 40 |
+| **total** | **240** (hard cap 250) |
+
+Resampling is not fitting: 2000 per-file joint replicates, 2000 band-selection
+paired replicates, 10 000 file-level replicates, 400 block-variance-curve
+replicates.  Development was executed twice (352 executions) for amendment A4;
+that is a resource figure, not a second evaluation.
+
+## 7a. Independent recomputation
+
+`scripts/recompute_t22.py` re-implements the declared combination from scratch
+--- the two-stage bootstrap, the continuity-corrected two-sided p, Holm's
+step-down and the verdict rule --- reading only the archived per-file draw
+arrays and the frozen configuration, never the runner's own combined block or
+this report.  It reproduces every interval, every p-value and all three
+verdicts exactly, and it prints what each verdict would have been without the
+dependence rule: limited recovery **supported**, denoising benefit
+**supported**, metric contribution **not supported**.
+
+## 8. Checks that passed inside the run
+
+* B = 1 identity control on all six development stretches, tolerance 10⁻¹².
+* `quadrature-OF` reproduces the bin read to a maximum relative difference of
+  3.8 × 10⁻¹² over all eligible stretches — the diagonal-Fourier-weighting
+  identity on real data, again.
+* The band real view was checked against the corresponding columns of the full
+  isometric real view on every cell.
+* The runner derives the allocation offsets and asserts them against the
+  protocol JSON, so configuration and code cannot drift apart.
+* The fit enumeration is checked against the hard cap before any data file is
+  opened in each stage.
+* 31 implementation tests pass (`tests/test_mlst_t22_narrowband.py`): split
+  overlap and hold-out disjointness, Fourier and physical-amplitude
+  conventions, band isometry and whitening metric, DC/Nyquist rejection, the
+  identity control and its failure mode, OF/bin-read equality, identical
+  PCA/EMPCA preprocessing with metric-only difference, calibration-only `k_inj`,
+  the A4 second-line rule on a leakage skirt and on a real second tone, joint
+  bootstrap logic and determinism, candidate pairing in the band bootstrap, the
+  selection rule and its blocked branches, Holm, the hierarchical bootstrap, and
+  the budget enumeration.
+
+## 9. Open questions for the local review
+
+1. **The dependence problem is not solved, and 300 evaluation windows were not
+   enough.**  Nine complete blocks at b = 32 is the same limiting count as the
+   whole-window stage.  Either a longer evaluation stretch or a different
+   dependence treatment is needed before any of these three claims can be
+   declared.  How much longer is a question this run does not answer: the
+   variance is still rising at the top of the grid, so the correlation length
+   is not bounded by this data.
+2. **Four eligible final-test files** is the declared minimum.  The equal-file
+   t-interval includes zero on every contrast; the two-stage bootstrap excludes
+   it on three.  Which of those a referee should weigh more is a genuine
+   statistical question and is not settled here.
+3. **The metric contribution is absent and the structural explanation is post
+   hoc.**  Whether a band wide enough to carry PSD structure and narrow enough
+   to keep p/n small exists on this instrument is untested.
+4. **Temporal hold-out, not replication.**  Nothing here is independent-file
+   evidence.
+
